        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Pydro\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/48/1844_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Pydro:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>phantaskippy wrote:</b><br><blockquote>...you had to do the whole attack one damage type...\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nMaybe Rabit can clarify, but we already have a ruling that the damage has to be the same for every target.<a href=\"http://boardgamegeek.com/article/7485233#7485233\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">http://boardgamegeek.com/article/7485233#7485233</a>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Nice.</p>\n<p>I love &gt;G, they really don't seem to have a set ruling, it changes depending on the question, or when you ask it, or whatever.</p>",
