      {
        "id": 71686,
        "name": "Rabit",
        "username": "Rabit",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-08-31T07:07:46.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I think the issue here is one of when the question was asked. Seriously, that was less than a month after the game was first released (Sep 2011)! They didn't have a full understanding of the implications of rulings, how one card fully affected another, etc. at that time. Now, they have a far better understanding of the game's fundamental mechanics and how the cards interact. So, yeah, much like other games, things sometimes change as the game evolves and grows.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>(Seriously, have you looked at the early rulings for Magic: The Gathering? Scary stuff, there…  <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=9\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\"> )</p>",
